# Laravel (v0.12 rewrite)
# The `.env` FAMILY, not the name — see the editor/backup block below for why an
# enumeration is the wrong shape here.
# NOTE: `!.env.example` is correct to keep, but it is NOT what keeps that file in
# the repo — the file is TRACKED, and .gitignore has no effect on tracked files.
# Do not "simplify" the negation away on the theory that it is load-bearing, and
# do not shy off the family form believing it would drop the example file.
.env*
!.env.example
/node_modules
/public/build
/public/hot
/public/storage
/storage/*.key
/storage/pail
.phpunit.result.cache
_ide_helper.php
/auth.json

# Editor and backup siblings of ANY file, secret-bearing ones included. A backup
# carries the same secret as the file it copies, and a per-file enumeration is
# permanently one editor behind: `.env` was ignored here while `.env~`, `auth.json~`
# and `storage/*.key~` were all stageable (roundtable #316, found live on a peer
# install as a 4,339-byte `.env~`). The rules above name WHICH files are secret;
# these cover HOW an editor spells a copy of one, so a new secret file added above
# inherits the coverage instead of needing its own siblings enumerated.
*~
*.bak
*.orig
*.save
*.swo
*.tmp
